$ Beam-section test deck (bulk only). Expected values in tests/test_beam_sections.py are by hand.
$ All beams run along +x, 10 long. CORD2R 5: x = basic y, z = basic z (CD of grids 3, 4, 6, 7).
$ EID  1 PBARL BAR 2(z) x 3(y), X=(0,1,0) basic      -> y=(0,1,0)   z=(0,0,1)
$ EID  2 same, X=(1,0,1) in CD 5 (OFFT GGG)           -> v=(0,1,1)  y=(0,.71,.71) z=(0,-.71,.71)
$ EID  3 same X but OFFT BGG (X basic)                -> v=(1,0,1)  y=(0,0,1)  z=(0,-1,0)
$ EID  4 G0 = grid 5 (0,30,10)                        -> v=(0,0,10) y=(0,0,1)  z=(0,-1,0)
$ EID  5 WA=WB=(0,0,1) (OFFT GGG, CD 0)               -> beam line at z = 1
$ EID  6 OFFT GOO, WA=WB=(0,.5,0) in the element frame -> y=(0,0,1): line at z = 0.5
$ EID  7 CBEAM PBEAML BAR taper: z width 2, 3, 4 at x/L 0, .5, 1 (height 1)
$ EID  8 PBAR A=6 I1=4.5 I2=2 -> equivalent rectangle 2(z) x 3(y)
$ EID  9 PBEAM same, N1A=N1B=0.5 -> rectangle centred at y = 0.5
$ EID 10 PBARL CHAN, EID 11 PBARL TUBE, EID 12 CROD (no section), EID 13 PBARL BOX too thick (warned)
